 "method": "A group net draws about the same amount of ink edge whatever its family. A drawing's edge is counted on a 48-wide grid with the training pen (the cells where ink meets no ink), and a family's class is set by its mean edge: 12 characters to a net up to 265, 10 up to 330, 8 above. Each class is one training set (tmath12, tmath10 and tmath8 for math): its families in a fixed order, cut into consecutive groups whose sizes differ by at most one, as train/split_expert.py's contiguous partition cuts a set, so the trainer needs no change. Inside a family the characters are dealt, largest edge first, to the group with the least edge per place so far, so the groups a family spans are balanced. Writes font/term-TIER-partition.json; --check compares instead.",
